    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This section details the preliminary data analyses, specifically examining univariate and multivariate normalities using skewness and kurtosis values for various measures including FSCRS_reassure, BMI, and EDE-Q. The results indicated no severe violation of the normal distribution of the data.",
      "evidence_source": "Preliminary data analyses Univariate and multivariate normalities were examined by the values of skewness (Sk) and Kurtosis (Ku). The skewness values ranged from \u22120.14 to 0.96 (in the FSCRS_reassure and BMI, respectively), while the values of Kurtosis ranged from \u22120.22 to 1.56 (in EDE-Q and BMI, respectively). According to Kline [35], these results revealed that there was no severe violation of the normal distribution of the data (z-scores: SK<|3| and Ku<|8\u201310|).",
